      "level": 1,
      "content": "Example: Check if a Linked List is Sorted"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To check if a linked list is sorted in ascending order, we need to traverse the list."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the next node is smaller than the current node, we know the linked list is not sorted."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "But if each node is smaller than the next node right until the end of the linked list, then it is sorted. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Linked List",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Source Code"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1# method to check if a linked list is sorted \n2def is_sorted(self):\n3    # empty linked list is considered sorted\n4    if not self.head:\n5        return True\n6    current = self.head\n7        \n8    # traverse the linked list\n9    while current.next:\n10        # if current node is greater than next\n11        # the linked list is unsorted\n12        if current.data > current.next.data:\n13            return False\n14        current = current.next\n15    return True"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Linked List: 3->5->2->12->16->None\nIs sorted?: False"
    },
